FinQuest System Architecture

1. Client Layer
- Web UI (React/Vue)
- Mobile Apps (iOS/Android)
- Auth flow (OAuth2 / JWT)

2. API Layer
- API Gateway (rate limit, auth, routing)
- REST/GraphQL endpoints
- Request validation

3. Services Layer
- Account Service (user profiles, KYC)
- Portfolio Service (holdings, performance)
- Market Data Service (price feeds, news)
- Order Service (trade execution, order book)
- Analytics Service (risk, recommendations)

4. Data Layer
- SQL DB for transactional data (Postgres)
- NoSQL for time series/cache (Redis, Mongo)
- Data warehouse (Snowflake / BigQuery)
- Audit logs (append-only)

5. Integration
- Brokerage/exchange APIs
- Payment/Gateway APIs
- 3rd-party market data providers

6. Infrastructure
- Kubernetes for deployment
- CI/CD pipeline
- Monitoring/alerting (Prometheus/Grafana)
- Secrets management (Vault)

7. Security
- TLS in transit
- Encryption at rest
- Role-based access control
- Fraud detection module

8. Non-functional
- High availability, autoscaling
- Disaster recovery/backup
- Observability/logging

Use this as blueprint for implementing FinQuest system architecture.

